{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=July 2014}}
{{Use British English|date=July 2014}}
Group B of the [[2014 FIFA World Cup]] consisted of both finalists of [[2010 FIFA World Cup|the previous World Cup]] in [[Spain national football team|Spain]] (defending champions), the [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]] (previous runners-up), [[Chile national football team|Chile]], and [[Australia men's national soccer team|Australia]]. Play began on 13 June and ended on 23 June 2014. The Netherlands and Chile progressed to the knockout stage, while Australia and Spain were eliminated after suffering two defeats in their opening two matches. Chile were eliminated by hosts [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]] in the round of 16 on [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalties]], while the Netherlands made their way to the semi-finals in which they lost to eventual runners-up [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]], also on penalties. The Netherlands won the match for third place with a convincing 3–0 victory against Brazil.

